# Binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
# Built binaries at the module roots (not the cmd/ source dirs).
#
# Every cmd/ package is listed, not just the two servers. A 19 MB Linux ELF of
# cmd/seeddev rode into the repo inside an unrelated dispatch fix on 2026-07-22
# and sat there tracked, because this list named only the binaries anyone
# happened to have built at the time. These are all reproducible with a single
# go build (and the Makefile targets go run them, so none is needed on disk).
/shingo-edge/shingoedge
/shingo-core/shingocore
/shingo-core/seeddev
/shingo-core/simcalc
/shingo-core/schemasnapshot
/shingo-core/defaultssnapshot
/shingo-edge/schemasnapshot
/shingo-edge/defaultssnapshot
build/

# Database files
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Config files (may contain secrets)
shingocore.yaml
shingoedge.yaml
*.env
.env
.env.*

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html
coverage
coverage-*
test-*.log
*.patch

# Go module cache (local builds)
.cache/
**/.cache/

# Temp / scratch files
scene.json
scene.txt

# Go workspace
# go.work is committed (see shared/ module + AI-agent resolution rationale
# in docs/ui-style-guide.md). go.work.sum is ignored — it tracks indirect
# dependency hashes that drift with local toolchain versions.
go.work.sum

# Vendor (dependencies fetched by go mod)
vendor/
# …except the web-asset vendor dir: Chart.js + plugins are committed and
# //go:embed-ed into the binary for air-gapped plant deploys (no CDN). See
# plan-mission-telemetry-v1 §6.
!shingo-core/www/static/vendor/
!shingo-core/www/static/vendor/**

# API reference docs (scraped, not source)
seer-docs/

# Python artifacts (for any utility scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Debug logs
shingo-debug*.log
**/shingo-debug*.log

# Personal notes
*.notes.md

# Planning docs and reference PDFs
payload-plan.md
API_Docs.pdf
docs/order-patterns

# AI agent config
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
**/.claude/

# scripts/gate.sh docker logs. PER-WORKTREE on purpose — they used to be one
# shared /tmp path that concurrent lanes truncated out from under each other.
.gate/

# Gate run artifacts (container logs, scope output) — build output, never source
.gate/

# Shard planner scratch: package list, per-shard logs, recorded timings.
# Written by scripts/gate.sh-adjacent CI tooling and by local rehearsals.
.shard/
.shard-artifacts/
